From: Security Audit <audit@ka9q-radio.local>
Date: Fri, 8 Aug 2026 12:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] Fix missing NULL check in hid-libusb new_hid_device()

The new_hid_device() function allocates a HID device structure with
calloc() but only uses assert() for error checking. This is removed
in release builds, leading to NULL pointer dereference.

This patch adds proper NULL checking and cleanup on failure.

Bug: Critical - NULL pointer dereference
Risk: Crash when opening USB HID devices with low memory
---
 src/hid-libusb.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/hid-libusb.c b/src/hid-libusb.c
index 1234567..abcdef0 100644
--- a/src/hid-libusb.c
+++ b/src/hid-libusb.c
@@ -131,8 +131,13 @@ static int return_data(hid_device *dev, unsigned char *data, size_t length);

 static hid_device *new_hid_device(void)
 {
-	hid_device *dev = calloc(1, sizeof(hid_device));
-	assert(dev != NULL);
+	hid_device *dev = calloc(1, sizeof(hid_device));
+	if(dev == NULL){
+		LOG("new_hid_device: calloc failed\n");
+		return NULL;
+	}
+
+	// Initialize synchronization primitives
 	dev->blocking = 1;

 	pthread_mutex_init(&dev->mutex, NULL);
--
